          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The broken tap prompts Nia to water the seedlings and shelter them when the shade cloth falls; the ending shows them protected, though the sequence reads more like a task log than a developed story.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia responds to thirsty seedlings and a fallen shade cloth, and the final image confirms they are protected; repetitive phrasing and the sunflower detour make the episode feel list-like.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000058\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The garden problems lead to watering and an improvised shelter, with the seedlings safe at the end; the plain, repetitive account offers little narrative development.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia waters the seedlings and shelters them after the shade cloth falls; the completed repairs provide closure, but the events are presented as a sequence of chores.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000036\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The seedlings are watered and covered while the tap and shade cloth are repaired, ending with them protected; the orderly but repetitive report has limited story-like momentum.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia addresses the broken-tap and fallen-cloth problems, and the final image shows the seedlings under repaired shade; the prose remains procedural and repetitive.\",\"group_id\":0}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":1,\"ending\":1,\"language\":2,\"overall\":1},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All six stories share the same garden problem and resolution: Nia waters thirsty tomato seedlings despite a broken tap, shelters them when the shade cloth falls, and the adults repair the equipment. Differences such as the order of repairs or wording in s000014, s000023, and s000036 do not create materially distinct plots.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Nia uses a watering can to address thirsty seedlings, improvises shelter after the shade cloth falls, and adults repair the tap and shade cloth; the seedlings end protected.\"}] }",
          "type": "output_text",
